# IMP-16 (CR-003, CRR-006, API/E2E F-1) an iOS seek starts its own ranged read unless the running fetch comes within 0.7 s
# command: TEST_RUNNER_AUTOBYTEUS_574_VIDEO=<a 60 s MP4> xcodebuild ... -only-testing:AutoByteusMobileCoreTests test (own simulator);
#   red: AuthorizedMediaLoaderReadAheadTests with AuthorizedMediaLoader.swift as at fe62667935 (IR-005), restored after;
#   diagnosis (temporary, deleted): a Core test that plays a 120 s 1.88 MB M4A through the loader at 60 KB/s and seeks to
#   60 s in code, on the fix and on IR-005; a temporary UI probe of the audio screen's sliders; loader read logging;
#   real node: native-video-node.mjs at the LAN address (two stacks; the pairing link is one-time), builds of this
#   commit (server, build:mobile-web); NativeMediaRealNodeUITests and NativeVideoRealNodeUITests via xcodebuild
#   test-without-building, testCAnM4AOverASlowerLinkSeeksByRange also on IR-005's loader (red)
# commit: 243d269420 (loader), 216bc68baf (the real-node test's scrubber)
# env: Xcode 26.1.1, iOS 26.1 simulator (iPhone 17, created for this round and deleted after); the worktree's node behind
#   the stack's proxy (1.5 MB/s; 60 KB/s and 50 ms for the M4A test; 50 ms for 574's delivery test)
# date: 2026-11-25
# result: Pass.
#   - The loader bug is real, shown in code: on IR-005 a seek to 60 s in a 60 KB/s M4A took about 14 s (the await) and no
#     read from the middle went out (the stream from 0 only); on the fix a read from bytes=951831- went out within 0.6 s and
#     the idle stream stopped at 196608 bytes.
#   - A defect in the durable UI test, found on the way (Rule 9, fixed as its own commit 216bc68baf): on the audio screen
#     app.sliders.firstMatch is AVKit's volume slider (identifier "Volume Slider", label "Current position"), so
#     testCAnM4AOverASlowerLinkSeeksByRange moved the volume and no seek happened, on either loader. It now takes the slider
#     whose identifier is "Current position". The scrub then lands at 60 s of 120 s.
#   - A gap in the first version of the fix, found by the corrected test: AVKit's scrubber seeks during the drag; a fetch an
#     early point started had no rate of its own yet, so it got the 1 MB cap and the final point waited on it. A fresh fetch
#     is now judged by the link's last measured rate (unit case 3).
#   - Unit cases: a read beyond the fetch's reach at its rate starts its own fetch and the idle one stops; a read within it
#     waits; a second seek before the first seek's fetch has a rate starts its own. The first and third are red on IR-005.
#     The Core suite passes 91 of 91; the AVPlayer test with a 60 s video still makes 3 requests and reopens from the cache.
#   - Real node: testCAnM4AOverASlowerLinkSeeksByRange passes (reads from 693716- during the drag and 964624- at its end);
#     red on IR-005's loader (only the stream from 0). The rest of NativeMediaRealNodeUITests passes, node removal last.
#     574: testAWideVideoFromTheChatLink (the scrub) and testBDeliversInRealTimeOverASlowerLink at 50 ms pass on a fresh stack
#     (13762562 bytes delivered in 10 s, 5347659 needed). Every media request carries the phone credential in its header;
#     none in a URL (47 on stack 1, 4 on stack 2).
#   - Not here: the 574 video test run that failed in the first combined run did so because xcodebuild runs classes in name
#     order and the audio class's testZ had removed the node; rerun on a fresh stack, it passes.

